Z||000000||fiero56||01-14-2001||01:06 AM||||Looking for pictures of black lace wheels with chrome lug nuts for reference.<P>I have spent probably a combined total of 16+ hours searching for my lost McGuard wheel lock key to no avail. I figure Tuesday I will look for a place willing to remove the wheel locks(which, by the way are torqued to 100 ft/lbs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> ). I have decided to replace all lugs with new ones. I see McGuard has some nice lug nuts available in two colors that I like, chrome and black in the bulge style( <A HREF="http://h07-1-1-00-0578.beready.att.net/automotive/lug_coneseat.html" TARGET=_blank>http://h07-1-1-00-0578.beready.att.net/automotive/lug_coneseat.html</A>  ).<BR>Just wondering if anyone has any pictures of chrome lugs on black lace wheels, so I can decide if I like the look or not.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-14-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||01-14-2001||08:38 AM||||Just a note - the factory specs for torque on the lugs is 100 ft-lbs.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||01-14-2001||09:37 AM||||I know the spec is 100 ft/lbs, that's why I torqued them that high, but locking lugs are usually torqued lower, I always make sure mine are torqued properly, to make it difficult to remove them without the key. Since the locking lugs on mine are chrome-plated(nickel-chromium if you want to get technical), which will make it diffcult to tack-weld anything on them. The shop will have to come up with something..||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||01-14-2001||10:12 AM||||Like this? The center caps are from Rodney Dickman.<P><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wheel_5.jpg">   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1986SE.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">   <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||01-14-2001||12:10 PM||||That's exactly what I was looking for, Oreif! Strange, but I thought of your car when I posted this, but I thought you had black lugs on your wheels. I figure when spinning, the silver lug nuts will look pretty good with the silver lip on the outside of the wheels.<P>Have you always had silver ones on your wheels, or did you add them recently? Are those cross-drilled rotors I see? I didn't know you had those on either.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||01-14-2001||12:57 PM||||I have always had the chrome ones. I like the chrome better than the black. It highlights the wheels better. (In my opinion)The center caps from Rodney make the wheels look good too! (I don't like the all silver center caps)(personal preference) Yes I have cross-drilled rotors. It was the kit from the Fiero Store. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
